\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.4}{\ignorespaces BDT output distribution on data for electrons with $p_T>10$ GeV from Z boson decays at $\sqrt {s} = 13$~TeV. MC distributions are normalized to the data.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.12}
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.5}{\ignorespaces ROC curves of the identification classifier for each training category with working point efficiencies marked by a diamond. The red curves correspond to the improved classifier used in the analysis, while the light blue curves show a retraining of the legacy MVA MC samples at $\sqrt {s} = 13$~TeV.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.14}
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.6}{\ignorespaces ROC curves for the electron multivariate identification (Boosted Decision Trees) compared with the cut-based selection working points for 8~TeV. Signal from Drell-Yan Monte Carlo simulation sample. Background from jets faking electrons in a data sample dominated by Z+jets. Electron candidates with $>$ 20 \GeV are shown. Left: Barrel. Right: Endcap\relax }}{10}{figure.caption.16}
