\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.57}{\ignorespaces Results of the differential cross section measurement for different observables. The predictions from {\sc powheg+JHUgen} and {\sc minloHJJ} are shown in blue and yellow, respectively. The central value of the measurement is obtained using the efficiencies from the {\sc powheg+JHUgen} gg$\rightarrow $H model with m(H)= 125 $\GeV $, and the error bar represents the combined statistical and systematic uncertainty. The grey box represents the additional uncertainty incurred when using different models to unfold the observed data distribution back to particle level. The fraction of $4e,4\mu $ and $2e2\mu $ in each bin are fixed to their SM expectations. \relax }}{120}{figure.caption.794}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(a)}{\ignorespaces {$\ensuremath {p_T}(\mathrm {H})$}}}{120}{figure.caption.794}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(b)}{\ignorespaces {$\mathrm {m}(\mathrm {Z}_{2})$}}}{120}{figure.caption.794}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(c)}{\ignorespaces {$|y(\mathrm {H})|$}}}{120}{figure.caption.794}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(d)}{\ignorespaces {$|\qopname \relax o{cos}\theta ^{*}|$}}}{120}{figure.caption.794}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(e)}{\ignorespaces {N(jets)}}}{120}{figure.caption.794}
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.58}{\ignorespaces Results of the differential cross section measurement for different observables. The predictions from {\sc powheg+JHUgen} and {\sc minloHJJ} are shown in blue and yellow, respectively. The central value of the measurement is obtained using SM efficiencies where the gg$\rightarrow $H prediction is from {\sc powheg+JHUgen} with m(H)= 125 $\GeV $, and the error bar represents the combined statistical and systematic uncertainty. The grey box represents the additional uncertainty incurred when using different models to unfold the observed data distribution back to particle level. In this case, this model-dependance uncertainty is assessed by taking into account the experimental constraints from the exiting CMS measurements, as discussed in Section~\ref {sec:totalZZXSecSyst}. The fraction of $4e,4\mu $ and $2e2\mu $ in each bin are allowed to float in the fit. \relax }}{122}{figure.caption.801}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(a)}{\ignorespaces {$\ensuremath {p_T}(\mathrm {H})$}}}{122}{figure.caption.801}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(b)}{\ignorespaces {$\mathrm {m}(\mathrm {Z}_{2})$}}}{122}{figure.caption.801}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(c)}{\ignorespaces {$|y(\mathrm {H})|$}}}{122}{figure.caption.801}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(d)}{\ignorespaces {$|\qopname \relax o{cos}\theta ^{*}|$}}}{122}{figure.caption.801}
\contentsline {subfigure}{\numberline {(e)}{\ignorespaces {N(jets)}}}{122}{figure.caption.801}
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.59}{\ignorespaces Results of the differential cross section measurement for different observables when the asimov dataset is generated assuming pure ZH production with cross section equal to the total SM cross section. The prediction for this pure ZH model is shown in red. The central value of the measurement is obtained using SM efficiencies with the gg$\rightarrow $H prediction from {\sc powheg+JHUgen} with m(H)= 125 $\GeV $, and the error bar represents the combined statistical and systematic uncertainty. The grey box represents the additional uncertainty incurred when using different models to unfold the observed data distribution back to particle level. \relax }}{124}{figure.caption.808}
